-    <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
+    <h2>1. Privacy by Design &amp; Data Minimization</h2>
     <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is built on the principles of privacy by design, data minimization, purpose limitation, and transparency by default. You can browse and read all news articles, reports, and multimedia content without creating an account or providing personal data.</p>
+    <p>When you choose to create an account or sign in, we collect only the minimum credentials required to authenticate your session (your chosen username—which may be a pseudonym—and password). We do not collect unnecessary personal identifiers such as your full name, date of birth, phone number, or physical address, and we never repurpose authentication data for marketing or profiling.</p>
     
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
+    <h2>2. Third-Party Scripts &amp; Tracking Mitigation</h2>
+    <p><strong>Zero third-party behavioral tracking</strong></p>
+    <p>We do not load third-party behavioral analytics trackers or invasive advertising scripts across our layout or authentication pages. External resources (such as typography from Google Fonts) are loaded with strict referrer and cross-origin controls (<code>referrerpolicy="no-referrer"</code> and <code>crossorigin="anonymous"</code>) so your browsing path is not leaked to external providers.</p>
     
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <h2>3. Cookies, Session Storage &amp; Security Headers</h2>
+    <p><strong>First-party session cookies</strong></p>
+    <p>Our website uses strictly necessary first-party session storage to maintain your saved reading list. We do not store sensitive authentication tokens or personally identifiable information (PII) in <code>localStorage</code>. All pages are delivered with strict privacy-preserving HTTP headers, including <code>Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin</code>, a defensive <code>Permissions-Policy</code> disabling camera, microphone, and geolocation access by default, and a strict <code>Content-Security-Policy</code>.</p>
+
+    <h2>4. Your Data Rights &amp; Control</h2>
+    <p><strong>Access, correction, and deletion</strong></p>
+    <p>You have full control over your data. You can view and remove saved reading list items directly from the Reading List menu at any time, and you may request account erasure or credential updates without losing access to public journalism on The DevTools Times.</p>
